id=a52sxq_settings_search_cold_start
name=Settings search: hidden settings stay hidden when Settings was not running
author=CodesRahul96
description=Found on 9.3.72 (search crash report "extra di"): every time Settings search opens, SecSettingsIntelligence refreshes its index and asks the Settings content provider which entries are unavailable on this device (non_indexables_key). When the Settings process is not running (killed in the background, force-stopped, first search from the home screen), the provider call starts it and arrives on a binder thread before SettingsApplication's background init has set the Spa environment; SearchFeatureProviderImpl's lazy indexable list then throws "UnsupportedOperationException: Spa environment is not set" (SpaSearchRepository.getSearchIndexablePageList), 20 ms before the environment is set. SettingsIntelligence treats the failed query as "no unavailable entries" and re-enables every hidden Settings row: 704 rows of 155 pages on the A52s (Privacy display / Maximum privacy protection, DeX, Dock, fingerprint/face entries of other models, developer pages, ...), until the next search with Settings already running hides them again. 1) SecSettings: getSearchIndexablePageList waits (off the main thread only, at most 3 s, normally a few ms) for the Spa environment instead of failing (K4SpaEnvWait). 2) SecSettingsIntelligence: a non-indexable query that returns no cursor (provider failed or unavailable) keeps the previous availability of that provider's rows instead of enabling all of them (PreIndexDataCollector.getNonIndexablesKeys returns null, add*NonIndexablesKeysFromRemoteProvider skip the authority). A provider that answers with an empty list still enables its rows, as stock.
